WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.417
After you understand the data and reconcile legacy problems, stable rules can move closer to data entry.

00:00:07.417 --> 00:00:10.627
NOT NULL protects required values.

00:00:10.627 --> 00:00:13.972
CHECK can enforce a pattern or domain.

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:18.102
UNIQUE can protect a field that truly must be unique.

00:00:18.102 --> 00:00:21.067
Foreign keys protect relationships.

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:27.942
Constraints prevent known defects from reappearing, but they should reflect real business rules.

00:00:27.942 --> 00:00:35.277
Connect this idea to a healthcare pipeline validating contact, demographic, and event fields.

00:00:35.277 --> 00:00:41.462
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:41.462 --> 00:00:49.787
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:49.787 --> 00:00:55.517
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:55.517 --> 00:01:01.569
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
